---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
import { Button } from '../../../src/components/button/Button'
import ComponentGrid from '../components/ComponentGrid.astro'
import { Thumbs } from '../../../src/components/thumbs/Thumbs'
import { Badge } from '../../../src/components/badge/Badge'
import { ListItem } from '../../../src/components/list-item/ListItem'
import { kit, built, tokens, readRepo, GITHUB } from '../lib/kit'
import { readFileSync } from 'node:fs'
import { pathToFileURL } from 'node:url'

const variants = kit.reduce((n, e) => n + (e.c.variants?.length ?? 0), 0)
const count = (files: Record<string, unknown>) => Object.keys(files).length
const icons = count(import.meta.glob('../../../assets/icons/*.svg'))
const illustrations = count(import.meta.glob('../../../assets/illustrations/*.svg'))

// What the step and foundation cards show: the real files, never a drawing
// made for the card. Read when the site builds.
const two = (n: number) => String(n).padStart(2, '0')
const contractLines = readRepo('contracts/button.contract.yaml').split('\n').slice(2, 9).join('\n')
const css = readRepo('src/components/button/button.css')
const cssLines = css.slice(css.indexOf('.rost-button {')).split('\n').slice(0, 7).join('\n')
declare const __REPO__: string
const figmaShot = `data:image/png;base64,${readFileSync(new URL('baseline/button/20-13.png', pathToFileURL(__REPO__))).toString('base64')}`
// By CSS variable: tokens.json keys lose the hyphen in `non-interactive`.
const swatches = ['actions/primary/default/background', 'interactive/inactive/hover/background', 'non-interactive/foreground/primary', 'non-interactive/foreground/negative/base'].map((k) => ({ k, v: `var(--${k.replaceAll('/', '-')})` }))
const iconSvgs = ['arrow-left', 'chevron-right', 'circle-outline', 'arrow-up', 'chevron-down', 'up-right'].map((n) => readRepo(`assets/icons/${n}.svg`).replace(/fill="#[0-9a-fA-F]{6}"/g, 'fill="currentColor"'))
const statuses = ['skeleton', 'draft', 'review', 'stable']
const roadmap = readRepo('docs/ROADMAP.md')
const nowAt = roadmap.indexOf('## Now: make the contracts')
const nextItems = [...roadmap.slice(nowAt, roadmap.indexOf('\n## ', nowAt + 5)).matchAll(/^\d+\. \*\*(.+?)\*\*/gm)].slice(0, 3).map((m) => m[1].replace(/\.$/, ''))
---
<Base title="Rost · My design system" description="Rost started as a design system for my own needs and grew into a product of its own. Today it serves products across different industries.">
  <section class="hero" data-paper>
    <canvas class="paper" aria-hidden="true"></canvas>
    <div class="kicker">Design system</div>
    <h1>Rost</h1>
    <p class="lede">Rost started as a design system for my own needs and grew into a product of its own. Today it serves products across different industries.</p>
    <p class="muted"><i lang="ro">Rost</i> is the Romanian word for purpose or order, in the sense that something is where it belongs.</p>
    <div class="btns">
      <Button href="/components/">Browse components</Button>
      <Button variant="secondary" href={GITHUB} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">GitHub</Button>
    </div>
    <div class="count">
      <div><b>{kit.length}</b><span>contracts</span></div>
      <div><b>{built.length}</b><span>built in code</span></div>
      <div><b>{variants}</b><span>variants</span></div>
      <div><b>{Object.keys(tokens).length}</b><span>tokens</span></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <ol class="cards steps" role="list">
    <li>
      <Thumbs as="div" className="card-thumb" number={two(1)} name="A contract" industry="Step" kind="YAML" showPeriod={false}>
        <span class="peek" aria-hidden="true"><pre class="file">{contractLines}</pre></span>
      </Thumbs>
      <p>Each component is one YAML file: its parts, its tokens, every variant, how to use it, and where my apps build it. It's the source. Figma was where it started.</p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <Thumbs as="div" className="card-thumb" number={two(2)} name="Code from the contract" industry="Step" kind="CSS and React" showPeriod={false}>
        <span class="peek" aria-hidden="true"><pre class="file">{cssLines}</pre></span>
      </Thumbs>
      <p>The CSS is written straight from the contract, so nobody types a colour by hand. The React component follows the same parts.</p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <Thumbs as="div" className="card-thumb" number={two(3)} name="Checked against Figma" industry="Step" kind="Visual test" showPeriod={false}>
        <span class="peek" aria-hidden="true">
          <span class="pair">
            <span class="half"><img src={figmaShot} alt="" width="76" height="48" /><span class="cap">Figma</span></span>
            <span class="half"><Button as="span">label</Button><span class="cap">Code</span></span>
          </span>
        </span>
      </Thumbs>
      <p>Each variant of a built component is rendered in Chrome and compared with Figma's own screenshot. A wrong colour or a missing icon fails it. Text edges get a little slack, because Figma and Chrome never draw them quite the same.</p>
    </li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Components</h2>
  <p class="muted">{built.length} of them are in code so far, and their cards show the real thing. The rest are contracts, and they come next, one at a time.</p>
  <ComponentGrid />

  <h2>Foundations</h2>
  <ul class="cards" role="list">
    <li>
      <Thumbs className="card-thumb" href="/tokens/" number={two(1)} name="Tokens" industry="Foundation" kind={`${Object.keys(tokens).length} tokens`} showPeriod={false}>
        <span class="peek" aria-hidden="true">
          <span class="swatches">{swatches.map(({ k, v }) => <span class="sw-row"><span class="chip-c" style={`background:${v}`} /><span class="cap">{k}</span></span>)}</span>
        </span>
      </Thumbs>
    </li>
    <li>
      <Thumbs className="card-thumb" href="/icons/" number={two(2)} name="Icons and illustrations" industry="Foundation" kind={`${icons} icons, ${illustrations} illustrations`} showPeriod={false}>
        <span class="peek" aria-hidden="true"><span class="icons">{iconSvgs.map((svg) => <span class="ico" set:html={svg} />)}</span></span>
      </Thumbs>
    </li>
    <li>
      <Thumbs className="card-thumb" href="/docs/contract/" number={two(3)} name="How a contract works" industry="Docs" kind="Statuses" showPeriod={false}>
        <span class="peek" aria-hidden="true"><span class="ladder">{statuses.map((st) => <Badge status={st === 'stable' ? 'positive' : 'default'}>{st}</Badge>)}</span></span>
      </Thumbs>
    </li>
    <li>
      <Thumbs className="card-thumb" href="/docs/roadmap/" number={two(4)} name="What's next" industry="Docs" kind="Roadmap" showPeriod={false}>
        <span class="peek" aria-hidden="true"><span class="next">{nextItems.map((t, i) => <ListItem as="span" selected={i === 0}>{t}</ListItem>)}</span></span>
      </Thumbs>
    </li>
  </ul>
</Base>

<script is:inline data-ids={JSON.stringify(kit.map((e) => e.id))}>
  // The old site was one long page with #badge-style anchors. Send those to
  // the new pages, but only the ones that exist.
  const known = JSON.parse(document.currentScript?.dataset.ids ?? '[]')
  const id = location.hash.slice(1)
  if (known.includes(id)) location.replace(`/components/${id}/`)
</script>

<style>
  .hero { position: relative; padding: var(--spacing-gap-large) 0 var(--spacing-gap-2xlarge); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .hero > :not(.paper) { position: relative; }
  /* The Paper effect, beside the words: a disc of dots, faded the way
     the portfolio site fades its own (solid to 40%, gone by 92%). It's up to 720px
     across, sized to the space between the text and the window's edge, then
     moved 280px in towards the text, and free to spill past the hero's top
     and bottom. Below 900px there's no room beside the text, so it goes. */
  .paper {
    --area: calc(100% + (var(--page-w, 100%) - 100%) / 2 - 600px);
    --d: min(720px, var(--area));
    position: absolute; pointer-events: none;
    width: var(--d); aspect-ratio: 1;
    left: calc(600px + var(--area) / 2 - var(--d) / 2 - 280px);
    top: 50%; transform: translateY(-50%);
    mask-image: radial-gradient(circle closest-side at 50% 50%, #000 40%, transparent 92%);
  }
  @media (max-width: 900px) { .paper { display: none; } }
  /* The step and foundation cards are Thumbs, laid out like the components'. */
  .cards { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: grid; gap: var(--spacing-gap-medium); grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(300px, 1fr)); }
  .cards :global(.card-thumb) { width: 100%; aspect-ratio: 384 / 334; }
  .steps p { margin: var(--spacing-gap-small-medium) 0 0; color: var(--fg-2); font-size: 15px; }
  /* The picture area, the same box Glimpse gives a component. */
  .peek { position: absolute; inset: 0 0 112px; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; padding: var(--spacing-gap-medium); overflow: hidden; }
  .file { margin: 0; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 11px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--fg-2); white-space: pre; overflow: hidden; max-width: 100%; }
  .pair { display: flex; gap: var(--spacing-gap-large); align-items: flex-end; }
  .half { display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; gap: var(--spacing-gap-small); }
  .half img { display: block; }
  .cap { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 11px; color: var(--fg-3); }
  .swatches { display: grid; gap: var(--spacing-gap-small); }
  .sw-row { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: var(--spacing-gap-small); }
  .chip-c { width: 20px; height: 20px; border-radius: var(--spacing-radius-xsmall); border: 1px solid var(--line); flex: none; }
  .icons { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 24px); gap: var(--spacing-gap-medium); color: var(--accent); }
  .ico :global(svg) { display: block; width: 24px; height: 24px; }
  .ladder { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: var(--spacing-gap-small); justify-content: center; }
  .next { display: grid; gap: var(--spacing-gap-2xsmall); width: 100%; max-width: 280px; }
  .next :global(.rost-list-item__label) { display: block; overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis; }
  .next :global(.rost-list-item), .next :global(.rost-list-item__start), .next :global(.rost-list-item__text) { min-width: 0; overflow: hidden; }
</style>

<script>
  import { mountPaper } from '../../../src/effects/paper'
  const hero = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-paper]')
  const canvas = hero?.querySelector<HTMLCanvasElement>('.paper')
  // The viewport's width without its scrollbar (100vw counts it), so the
  // paper spans the page and never makes it scroll sideways.
  const fit = () => document.documentElement.style.setProperty('--page-w', `${document.documentElement.clientWidth}px`)
  fit()
  addEventListener('resize', fit)
  if (hero && canvas) mountPaper(canvas, { area: hero, buttons: hero.querySelectorAll('.rost-button'), sketches: true, ripple: true, avoid: hero.querySelectorAll('.kicker, h1, .lede, .muted, .btns, .count') })
</script>
